   "title": "E3 1.0.0 -> 2.0.0",
   "summary": "E3 1.0.0 -> 2.0.0: the Fick aerobic envelope widened after a measured zebrafish broke it (Palstra et al. 2010, PMC3013094: MO2max at Ucrit 2630 mg O2 kg^-1 h^-1, about 2x the per-kg delivery v1 allowed). v2 bounds eta <= 0.23 (Gladman and Askew 2024) and O2 delivery Q*Ca <= 0.0187 ml O2/s at 0.06 kg (1600 mg O2 kg^-1 h^-1), ceiling 0.0458 -> 0.0833 W, wording rescoped from every teleost to its sources; v1 stays compiled and pinned by law sets 1.0.0-1.5.0, and v2 is proved a weakening of v1 (TeleostAerobic.toV2). Flying-fish powered-flight shortfall: 16x on the new envelope, about 10 to 29x (central about 20x) across corrected inputs, 38x with the original snapper proxies; still ruled out by an order of magnitude. perturb-current 1.1.0 adds a P2b scope assumption (aerobic only below about 0.8 Ucrit; taxon-appropriate ceiling); fick-principle 1.1.0 adds a scope note (taxon-appropriate MO2max or Q). The three new versions carry approval role carried-forward-pending-review: no person has reviewed them yet. Report: physics/FICK-CEILING-CHECK.md.",
