   "title": "perturb-pressure 1.0.0 -> 2.0.0",
   "summary": "perturb-pressure 1.0.0 -> 2.0.0: Boyle's law for a closed swim bladder now takes pressure from the water column, P(d) = p0 + rho g d, with p0, rho and g as named hypotheses (Delphi.Hydro.WaterColumn, lean/Delphi/Hydrostatics.lean). Version 1.0.0 fixed the gradient at 1 atm per 10 m; in sea water (1025 kg/m^3) the real gradient is 10053 Pa/m, below 10132.5, so v1 called a correct Boyle volume violated by 0.5 to 1 percent. The v1 case is the instance oneAtmPer10m. v1 is superseded, not deleted: law-versions/perturb-pressure@1.0.0.json, and its Lean statement stays compiled. Constraint P3 now uses Delphi.Hydro.closed_bladder_rules_out; 4 new statement mutants are rejected (61/61 overall, 19/19 controls).",
